The word "abandon" isn't quite fair—he can maintain obligations across distance. But the timing matters: his siblings may need help now, and a delayed benefit doesn't fully substitute for present need. So there's real tension, not a clean answer. The strongest reading is that he faced a genuine dilemma where reasonable people could weigh the claims differently. Pure "shape your own future regardless" underweights the concrete debt of sacrifice; pure "he abandoned them" underweights his legitimate autonomy and the possibility that education serves everyone.

